# Cursor Project Rules

The single source of truth for this project is `AI_CONTEXT.md` at the repo root.
Read it and follow it for the project summary, tech stack, folder structure, and
all coding conventions.

Key rules (full list in `AI_CONTEXT.md`):

- Match existing code style and `.editorconfig`; don't reformat unrelated code.
- Never hardcode secrets — use `.env` (gitignored). See `.env.example`.
- Don't add dependencies without the team agreeing; note any new dep in the PR.
- New features ship with at least one test.
- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` when behavior changes.
- If a requirement is unclear, leave a `TODO:` comment instead of guessing.

If this file and `AI_CONTEXT.md` disagree, `AI_CONTEXT.md` wins.
